Fenchurch Street railway station , also known as London Fenchurch Street , is a central London railway terminus in the southeastern corner of the City of London . It takes its name from its proximity to Fenchurch Street , a key thoroughfare in the City . The station and all trains are operated by c two c . Services run on lines built by the London and Blackwall Railway ( L and BR ) and the London , Tilbury and Southend Railway ( LTSR ) to destinations in east London and south Essex , including Upminster , Grays , Basildon , Southend and Shoeburyness . 
