`` On the Road Again '' is a song recorded by the American blues  minus  rock group Canned Heat in nineteen sixty-seven  . A driving blues  minus  rock boogie , it was adapted from earlier blues songs and includes mid minus nineteen sixty s psychedelic rock elements . Unlike most of Canned Heat 's songs from the period , second guitarist and harmonica player Alan Wilson provides the distinctive falsetto vocal . `` On the Road Again '' first appeared on their second album , Boogie with Canned Heat , in January nineteen sixty-eight  ; when an edited version was released as a single in April nineteen sixty-eight  , `` On the Road Again '' became Canned Heat 's first record chart hit and one of their best  minus  known songs . 
