The Cabinet of Doctor Caligari ( German : Das Cabinet des Doctor Caligari ) is a nineteen twenty  German silent horror film , directed by Robert Wiene and written by Hans Janowitz and Carl Mayer . Considered the quintessential work of German Expressionist cinema , it tells the story of an insane hypnotist ( Werner Krauss ) who uses a somnambulist ( Conrad Veidt ) to commit murders . The film features a dark and twisted visual style , with sharp  minus  pointed forms , oblique and curving lines , structures and landscapes that lean and twist in unusual angles , and shadows and streaks of light painted directly onto the sets . 
